// The control for the join: arms that answer different types are not a value
// this pass can print. One `instr` line carries one type, and
// `match n { 0 => 1 _ => "two" }` has two, so the rule refuses, E3001 says what
// is missing, and the file prints nothing.
//
// Answering `int` anyway would put a type on the read of `v` that the wildcard
// contradicts at run time -- the same class of defect that made
// `if_value_branch_types.orb` a refusal rather than a golden.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "fn bad(n: int) -> int { val v = match n { 0 => 1 _ => \"two\" } return v }"
    val output = compileFrontendSource("fixture", source)
    if output == "" {
        print("arms that disagree stay a give-up")
    }
}
